#### Trigger System

The STAR trigger system is based on a set of fast detectors, which includes ZDC, pVPD, TOF/CTB, BEMC, and BBC. The event selection relies on the measurement of the event multiplicity and energy distribution in pseudo-rapidity (\(\eta\)) and azimuth angle (\(\phi\)). The multiple level structure of the trigger system is based on TPC timing considerations, and consists of a Level 0 selection followed by Level 1, Level 2, and High Level Trigger for analysis and rejection. Each detector channel is digitized for every RHIC crossing and fed into a Data

